s round 1 but James already spoke, now Emily). We need to respond, referencing James's point, maybe agree or challenge. Use our own notes. We have notes on all candidates. We need to bring in evidence, maybe discuss other candidates. We should decide if we agree with James recommending B, or propose another candidate. Let's evaluate.\n\nWe have candidate facts: A can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks, regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. C can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to discuss criteria: reliability, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility. Also other criteria.\n\nWe might argue that Candidate C has strong decision quality, calm under pressure, technical competence, excellent attention, and puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation). However, difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric might be concerns. But \"puts concern for others above everything\" suggests good crew cooperation. Egocentric may conflict but maybe less severe. Also not willing to further education is a concern for adaptability.\n\nCandidate D has responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation and stress resilience.\n\nCandidate A has leadership, anticipation, spatial vision, but unfriendly and unhealthy (maybe reliability?).\n\nCandidate B has reliability and stress handling but communication issues and weak memory.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate is best overall. I think Candidate C might be strong: quick correct decisions, calm under pressure, technical competence, excellent attention, concern for others. The communication difficulty and egocentric are concerns, but maybe less severe than B's nasty remarks? B's nasty remarks could be harmful to crew. C's difficulty communicating ideas may affect crew but maybe can be mitigated. Also C's egocentric may be a problem. But \"puts concern for others above everything\" suggests crew cooperation.\n\nWe could argue that C is the strongest alternative and perhaps better than B because of decision quality and calmness, and his concern for others outweighs communication difficulty. So we could shift vote to C.\n\nWe need to reference James's point and provide evidence from our notes. Provide a concise argument.\n\nThus: \"I see value in B's reliability but I'm concerned about his communication; C offers strong decision making, calm under pressure, excellent attention, and a clear concern for others, which may outweigh his communication difficulty.\" Then vote for C.\n\nLet's produce public message: state provisional vote for Candidate C, reference James's recommendation, mention evidence: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation), technical competence (understands complicated technology). Also note concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Explain why still best.\n\nNow produce metadata JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
